### Pruebas manuales (extensión REST Client / Thunder Client de VS Code)
@base = http://localhost:8000

### Login estudiante (formulario OAuth2)
# @name loginAna
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

username=ana@uni.edu.co&password=Estudiante123*

### Login JSON (admin)
# @name loginAdmin
POST {{base}}/auth/login-json
Content-Type: application/json

{"correo": "admin@uni.edu.co", "contrasena": "Admin123*"}

### Login Carlos
# @name loginCarlos
POST {{base}}/auth/login-json
Content-Type: application/json

{"correo": "carlos@uni.edu.co", "contrasena": "Estudiante123*"}

@tokenAna = {{loginAna.response.body.access_token}}
@tokenAdmin = {{loginAdmin.response.body.access_token}}
@tokenCarlos = {{loginCarlos.response.body.access_token}}

### Registro de estudiante
POST {{base}}/auth/registro
Content-Type: application/json

{"nombres": "Laura", "apellidos": "Ruiz", "correo": "laura@uni.edu.co", "codigo_estudiantil": "2021777", "contrasena": "Clave123*", "id_programa": 1}

### Sin token -> 401
GET {{base}}/objetos

### Estudiante pide roles -> 403
GET {{base}}/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAna}}

### Admin lista roles
GET {{base}}/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAdmin}}

### Objetos disponibles
GET {{base}}/flujo/objetos-disponibles
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenCarlos}}

### 1. Ana publica un objeto
POST {{base}}/flujo/publicar-objeto
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAna}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"codigo": "OBJ-0100", "nombre": "Bata de laboratorio", "id_categoria": 6, "id_condicion": 2}

### 2. Carlos solicita el objeto 1
# @name solicitud
POST {{base}}/flujo/solicitar
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenCarlos}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"id_objeto": 1, "fecha_inicio_deseada": "2026-10-12", "fecha_fin_deseada": "2026-10-20", "mensaje": "Para el parcial de cálculo"}

### 3. Ana aprueba
POST {{base}}/flujo/solicitudes/{{solicitud.response.body.id_solicitud}}/decision
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAna}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"aprobar": true, "comentario": "Recógela en biblioteca"}

### 4. Ana registra la entrega (préstamo)
# @name prestamo
POST {{base}}/flujo/solicitudes/{{solicitud.response.body.id_solicitud}}/prestar
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAna}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Mis préstamos (Carlos)
GET {{base}}/flujo/mis-prestamos
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenCarlos}}

### 5. Devolución
POST {{base}}/flujo/prestamos/{{prestamo.response.body.id_prestamo}}/devolver
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAna}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"id_condicion_devolucion": 2, "observaciones": "Sin novedades"}

### CRUD: crear categoría (admin)
POST {{base}}/categorias
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAdmin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"nombre": "Tablets", "descripcion": "Tabletas"}

### Actualizar (ver que 'actualizado' cambia y 'creado' no)
PUT {{base}}/categorias/7
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAdmin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"descripcion": "Tabletas y iPads"}

### Borrado lógico (estado=false)
DELETE {{base}}/categorias/7
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAdmin}}

### Incluir inactivos (admin)
GET {{base}}/categorias?incluir_inactivos=true
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAdmin}}
